        "reviewNotes": "openspec added meaningful value: identified the precise defect (getGreeting() returns 'hello world' instead of 'hello dolly'), pinpointed the fix site in src/hello.ts, and correctly derived VCs from the story description since ACs were empty. Speckit was intentionally skipped per coordinator notes — a static greeting change has no security surfaces, edge cases, or integration points to harden, so a second agent would have added no non-overlapping value. Brownfield constraints respected: splitCount 0, acceptanceChanged false. Single-agent rationale is internally consistent with the story's complexity level.",
